1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,710
How do ordinary grains of sand

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:05,450
become a crystal-clear glass bottle?

3
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:09,800
The answer lies in an extraordinary transformation.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,300
It begins with three key ingredients.

5
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,980
Silica sand, soda ash and limestone.

6
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:21,060
Each plays an essential role

7
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:24,000
in creating strong, transparent glass.

8
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:27,600
Inside a powerful furnace,

9
00:00:27,930 --> 00:00:31,600
the mixture reaches around 1,500 degrees Celsius,

10
00:00:31,850 --> 00:00:34,500
melting into a glowing liquid.

11
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:39,200
Machines shape the molten glass into bottles.

12
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:44,550
They are then cooled gradually

13
00:00:44,570 --> 00:00:47,900
to prevent cracks and strengthen the finished product.

14
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:53,090
And remarkably, old glass can be recycled

15
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:55,450
and transformed into new products.

16
00:00:55,530 --> 00:00:57,250
From sand to bottle,

17
00:00:57,290 --> 00:00:59,700
glass begins a new life.
